  "title": "ARTEMIS II BOOSTER STACKING COMPILATION",
  "description": "Technicians with NASA's Exploration Ground Systems integrate segments on the agency's SLS (Space Launch System) Moon rocket boosters inside the Vehicle Assembly Building at NASA's Kennedy Space Center in Florida. The twin solid boosters, five segments on each side, will help support the remaining rocket components and the Orion spacecraft during final assembly of the Artemis II Moon rocket and provide more than 75 percent of the total SLS thrust during liftoff from NASA Kennedy’s Launch Pad 39B.",
